    <briefdescription>
<para>Training-module LoRA adapter for real weight manipulation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Manages a collection of named LoRA weight entries and provides:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Adding/removing adapter layers with configurable rank and alpha</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Applying individual or batched additive weight updates (no simulation)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>A real forward pass: output = (input @ B @ A) × scaling</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exporting/importing weight snapshots for checkpoint integration</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Initialization convention (per the LoRA paper, §3):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>B is Kaiming-uniform initialised (non-zero)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>A is zero-initialised (so the initial adapter output is exactly zero)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread-safety: NOT guaranteed. Callers must provide external synchronisation when sharing a single instance across threads.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The public API is stable; internal implementation is Pimpl. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
